<title>ARGENTINA: Santander, Argentine bank form mortgage co.</title>
<headline>Santander, Argentine bank form mortgage co.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Banco Santander and Buenos Aires province state-run Banco Provincia have signed an agreement in principle to form a mortgage loan company, Clarin newspaper reported Monday.</p>
<p>Both banks would have a 50 percent stake in the new firm, aimed at taking advantage of Argentina's growing home loan demand, it added in the report that did not quote any sources by name.</p>
<p>Santander last month took control of Agentina's Banco Rio, which has branches in other provinces, the report said.</p>
<p>No financial details were mentioned.</p>
<p>Neither Santander nor Provincia's officials were immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>((-- Guillemo Haskel, Buenos Aies newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
